window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Pain. Cold. Falling. Floating. And then, a set of emerald green eyes staring down at me.</p> <p>Death was supposed to be easy. It was what I’ve been longing for, what I’ve been working towards. The last thing I expected was for me to fight harder in death than I ever did in life.</p> <p>It’s been three months since I joined my mates in the Underworld. Three months of training my powers, my deadly affinity, with the blue-haired demon who likes to garden. But I still can’t defeat him.</p> <p>King Balthazar. The wretched Reaper King of the Third Circle who wishes to take me as his bride, trap me, and use my powers to his own advantage.</p> <p>I won’t let him have the chance.</p> <p>Finding some unlikely allies, me, my mates, a decaying witch, a servant, and a missing friend work to undermine the King at every turn until my powers are strong enough to finally bring him down.</p> <p>But I’m not prepared for what comes after.</p> <p>Death &amp; Decay is Book 2 in The Last Words Trilogy. Book 1, Glass &amp; Grim, must be listened to first to fully understand the story. This book includes mature themes and elements, so please be sure to see the content warnings before proceeding.</p>"; 
